---
import { ISSUES_URL } from "../config";
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms for downloading and using Social Media Agent."
  updated="September 28, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms apply when you download or use the Social Media Agent desktop
    app and this website. By using the app, you agree to them.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the app</h2>
  <p>
    You may install and use the app on your own computers to plan and draft your
    content. Don't use it to break the law, or to break the terms of services it
    connects to.
  </p>

  <h2>Your ChatGPT account and Codex</h2>
  <p>
    AI drafting runs through the Codex CLI on your ChatGPT account. You need
    your own ChatGPT plan that includes Codex. You are responsible for following
    OpenAI's terms and usage policies. Replies count toward your plan's limits,
    and OpenAI decides which models are available and when. The app includes a
    copy of the Codex CLI, which OpenAI provides under the Apache License 2.0.
    That license and other third-party notices ship with the app in its
    <code>resources\licenses</code> folder.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content</h2>
  <p>
    You own what you create in the app. AI-generated drafts can be wrong,
    unoriginal or unsuitable, so review everything before you publish it. You
    are responsible for what you post and for following Instagram's rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    Your data stays on your computer (see the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>). Keeping backups is up to you. The
    app can export everything to a file from Settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>
    The app downloads and installs updates automatically. We may change or stop
    offering features, or the app itself, at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The app is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, express or
    implied, including fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We
    don't guarantee that it will be error-free or always available, or that it
    won't lose data.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect,
    incidental, special or consequential damages, or for lost data, profits or
    content, arising from your use of the app.
  </p>

  <h2>Not affiliated</h2>
  <p>
    Social Media Agent is an independent project. It is not affiliated with,
    endorsed by or sponsored by OpenAI, Instagram or Meta. Their names and
    trademarks belong to their owners.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version, and
    continuing to use the app means you accept the changes.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions? <a href={ISSUES_URL}>Open an issue on GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
